{"ref":"BDB Aramaic, אֱסוּר","hw":"אֱסוּר","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">אֱסוּר</span></big>  <strong>n.</strong>[<strong>m.</strong>] <strong>band, bond (</strong>𝔗 <span dir=\"rtl\">אֲסוּר</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">אֵיסוּר</span>, Syriac <span dir=\"rtl\">ܐܶܣܳܪ</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ܐܰܣܽܘܪ</span> <strong>)</strong>;—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">א׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:12\" href=\"/Daniel.4.12\">Dn 4:12</a>, <a data-ref=\"Daniel 4:20\" href=\"/Daniel.4.20\">20</a> (of iron and bronze, for stump, in Neb.’s vision); pl. abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">אֱסוּרִין</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezra 7:26\" href=\"/Ezra.7.26\">Ezr 7:26</a> <em>bonds</em> = imprisonment.","next":"BDB Aramaic, אֱסָר","prev":"BDB Aramaic, אסר"}